# L §5.7 (refusals: "a place kind without its unit or sign rule", LOAD-PLACEKIND), the grammar ("unit and sign:
# required"), §8.3 (tally 2.1.7 R9's reach; the builder's STOP-REPORT, pick P44): a subkind of the root places whose
# chain states no unit and no sign is refused at its line, whatever the asks. refcore 2.1.7 loaded such a kind, and
# with parts clauses printed `LOAD-PARTS kind savings keeps parts and is None`.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons: parties
kind savings: places
  owned by arrive
  step minor(PLN)
  takes k for w order if k.owner == ania then 0 else 1
place konto: savings lives 2026-01-01..
def arrive[m in events, p in parties]: num at m.day
  rule base = if p == ania then 1 else 0
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-06-30)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ania] lives 1980-01-01..
  persons + [tomek] lives 1981-01-01..
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start
=== expect
refused: LOAD-PLACEKIND place kind savings has no unit or sign rule (m.tally:10)
